(MACRO Spindle warm-up)
(PARAM 1 rpm "Top speed" rpm 6000 min=100 max=24000)
(PARAM 2 seconds "Duration" time 240 min=20 max=1800)
(Runs the spindle up in four equal steps to the top speed, each step a quarter of the duration, then stops it.)
(Example macro of the lcnc-suite: edit it in the Macros tab or replace it.)
o<spindle_warmup> sub
  M73
  G97
  #<step> = 1
  o<warmup_steps> while [#<step> LE 4]
    M3 S[#1 * #<step> / 4]
    G4 P[#2 / 4]
    #<step> = [#<step> + 1]
  o<warmup_steps> endwhile
  M5
o<spindle_warmup> endsub
